  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-03-14T02:52:12.169Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "After seeing how well the tracking worked when using Selfie Expression from a friend, I noticed that a lot of immersion was lost thanks to the the speed at which their avatar updated the tracked bones (3hz-5hz?) which is the default Desktop mode limit. It somewhat discourages me from using it if desktop users are still gonna be updating their tracking that slowly. It's nice that the option is there, but feels bittersweet when the refresh rate is that slow.\n\nSure, when they don't have it enabled there is hardly a point to increase that limit, but could we get that limit increased so desktop users feel less 'robot movements' like? I think just 10hz would be more than acceptable, or anything smooth enough to be caught off-guard with a \"Whoa, you are not in VR?!\" moment.",
